WEBVTT

00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:06.910
I'm glad Erec-sama came 
home all safe and sound.

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:08.340
You think the wounds he got

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:09.980
fighting DT have already healed?

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:13.910
By the way, where exactly 
did he get hurt?

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:15.460
Variation, do you know?

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.680
Probably his soul.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:19.990
I see, he might not look that way,

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.000
but Erec-sama can be quite naive.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:22.690
You know that for a fact?

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:24.520
According to the 
image I have in my head.

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:26.550
When we were at his home,

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:28.000
Erec-sama kept laying into himself.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.680
What, he kept laying into himself?

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:33.520
It's not the kind of laying 
into that you're into.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.540
I would have been happy to console him.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:37.470
Oh, Erec-sama has a fiancée.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.460
What?!

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.570
But he's never laid a 
finger on Emilia-sama.

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:42.410
Ah, the teasing game.

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:43.470
Uh, no.

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:45.650
He doesn't want to 
since it's a political marriage.

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:46.660
That's definitely not it.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:48.830
Marriage is like ending your life.

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:50.620
How did that even come up?!

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:53.100
Well, I guess in times like these,

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.280
we should go to a hostess club.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:55.460
Hell no!

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:44.540
Hey!

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:46.180
I got some water.

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:48.460
Thanks, Kon.

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:53.280
Jeez, we've only got jerky 
and dried fruit left.

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:55.270
I am so sorry, princess.

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:58.600
I hope you will accept 
this humble offering.

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:00.260
Don't worry about it, Marian.

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:01.990
We'll get to a town tomorrow.

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:02.700
Huh?

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:06.130
Looks like you didn't 
properly calculate

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:07.870
the amount of food we'd need.

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:09.710
I guess not.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:10.740
Captain!

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:14.210
This oversight must be 
strictly rectified.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:18.380
Keep harping on this and 
you won't get dinner.

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:21.880
I thank you from the bottom of 
my humble heart for this food.

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:29.910
Sleeping outside and 
eating grub like this

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:32.070
really makes you yearn 
for civilization.

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:33.300
Hey, do we have soy sauce?

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:34.160
Soy sauce?

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:35.990
If only we had a convenience store!

00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:38.500
We could have hot oden 
soup, or rice balls.

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:40.170
And fried chicken on a stick.

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:41.490
And teen magazines.

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:43.870
What are you talking about?

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:45.250
You don't know about comics?

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:47.320
Of course you don't.

00:03:48.190 --> 00:03:50.520
That reminds me, whatever 
happened to Goten the 3rd?

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:53.590
Who won the Tenkaichi 
athletic tournament?

00:03:53.590 --> 00:03:55.680
Are you talking about your old world?

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:58.000
I haven't played a game in so long.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.690
I haven't watched any anime.

00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:01.230
I haven't eaten any junk food or candy.

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:02.880
We don't have those things, 
so what are you gonna do?

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:04.620
Let me just lay it out for y'all.

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:06.380
Back in my world,

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:09.750
I was a real dyed-in-the-wool 
anti-social gamer nerd!

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:12.310
That part of me screams,

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:14.520
"What the hell is this eating 
and sleeping in nature crap,

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.650
having to squeeze out wisdom

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:19.320
and courage and all sorts of stuff

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.740
to overcome dangers and other nuisances

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:24.280
day after day after day?"

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:28.210
What the hell are you saying?

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:31.940
I want to go home.

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:35.490
That's why you're traveling with us.

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:36.420
He's right.

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:37.670
Once we reach the capital,

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:39.710
I'm sure we'll find a 
way to get you home.

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:54.580
I really want to play some video games.

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:57.760
I bet a bunch of new 
ones have come out.

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:01.820
<i>Yes!</i>

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:07.930
I want to eat junk 
food and read comics.

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:11.010
I haven't watched any late-night 
anime lately either.

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:16.300
I wonder what happened on 
<i>Magical Wife Rirical Hanako</i>.

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:19.590
Maybe it already wrapped up.

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:22.770
That reminds me.

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:25.400
I wonder how much time has 
passed since I've gotten here?

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:26.730
About three months?

00:05:26.730 --> 00:05:30.850
Shouldn't this kind of anime 
be wrapped up in one season?

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:34.980
Let me go home, let me 
go home, let me go ho—

00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:37.810
Nobody can say it three 
times that fast!

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:44.650
There it is.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:48.700
It's pretty big!

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:49.750
Yeah!

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:52.570
I hope they have a lot 
of good restaurants.

00:05:52.570 --> 00:05:54.700
You want to eat first thing?

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:55.660
Lodging first.

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:58.370
I want to take a hot bath 
after all this time.

00:05:58.370 --> 00:05:59.330
Yes!

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:01.950
Let's find some nice lodging.

00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:05.960
Kon's pretty quiet today, huh?

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:13.300
You've been doing that
 since this morning.

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:14.560
Kon?

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:16.100
I'm finished.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:20.760
What is that?

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:22.860
Is that also something 
from civilization?

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:25.290
It's a controller.

00:06:32.920 --> 00:06:34.970
That feels marvelous.

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:40.120
I've got a new lease on life!

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:43.100
Hey, kids! No running in here!

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:44.630
Told ya.

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:50.330
Up, up, down, down, up, down, right!

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:51.800
It was up!

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:54.190
Down, down, down, down, 
down, down, down!

00:06:54.190 --> 00:06:56.590
Hey, Kon, the bath is empty right now.

00:06:56.590 --> 00:06:57.550
Why don't you go wash off your sweat.

00:06:57.550 --> 00:06:57.890
Nah.

00:06:59.110 --> 00:07:00.300
Up, go up!

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:01.760
Not bad!

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:02.490
Take this!

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:04.320
Right, right, left, 
 up, down, up, down!

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:05.170
Right there!

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:07.880
Up, up!

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:10.150
There, right there!

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:14.660
So that's what he was up to.

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:17.530
You mean he doesn't even want to eat?

00:07:17.530 --> 00:07:19.940
He told me to bring him back

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:21.670
some junk food and
 comics, if there are any.

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:24.180
What is this junk food he speaks of?

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:26.670
Is it different from normal sweets?

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:30.060
Apparently, it is not sweet, 
but either savory, or spicy,

00:07:30.060 --> 00:07:32.370
or comprised of strange flavors,

00:07:32.370 --> 00:07:35.150
often possessing properties of 
crunchiness or crispiness.

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:44.940
Hey, Kon!

00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:48.440
You wanted snacks, so we got you some.

00:07:48.890 --> 00:07:49.680
Yeah.

00:07:50.730 --> 00:07:52.240
What is he doing?

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:53.860
Uh...

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:56.080
I'm watching TV.

00:07:56.070 --> 00:07:57.160
TV?

00:07:57.660 --> 00:07:59.370
I'm watching 
<i>Space Masterpiece Theater:</i>

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:00.950
<i>The Little Princess Sara</i>.

00:08:01.470 --> 00:08:03.390
It's the part when her father dies

00:08:03.390 --> 00:08:05.660
and she gets taken in by her Uncle Ral.

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:08.930
This is so sad...

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:16.050
Look, Kon, we got you some 
famous snacks of this region.

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:20.470
Bees marinaded in syrup. 
Smoked rolly lizard tails.

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:22.350
Buttered momora larvae.

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:24.950
They're all crunchy and crispy 
and quite interesting.

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:29.490
That's not what I'm talking about!

00:08:30.140 --> 00:08:31.100
Whatever!

00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:32.860
I'm playing a game, 
so just leave me alone.

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:36.800
The important question now is, 
where did I save last?

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:40.660
See? Very strange.

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:43.670
He's got none of his normal energy.

00:08:43.670 --> 00:08:46.820
He just keeps randomly talking 
about the other world.

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:50.430
Maybe he remembered his home 
and it made him lonely.

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:51.870
Maybe he's homesick.

00:08:51.870 --> 00:08:54.050
Guess he's still a kid.

00:08:54.380 --> 00:09:00.140
Zap, zap! Be-be-be-
be-beam! Right there!

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:02.030
We have to do something, though.

00:09:02.030 --> 00:09:04.390
We can't just let him fall 
further into depression.

00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:07.650
He'll get sick if he 
doesn't eat something.

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:09.560
Up, up, up!

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:10.670
Bam!

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:12.840
Kon?

00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:14.950
All right!

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:16.980
I told you to leave me alone!

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:19.950
But you need to eat something.

00:09:20.390 --> 00:09:22.430
Is there anything you want?

00:09:22.430 --> 00:09:25.250
Then bring me a big hamburger meal.

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:26.920
From Smackdonalds.

00:09:27.260 --> 00:09:29.660
That's food from your home, right?

00:09:29.660 --> 00:09:31.230
Will you explain it to us?

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:34.460
It's a big hamburger with 
fries and chicken nuggets.

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:35.700
And a large cola.

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:36.930
Okay, Kon.

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:38.960
Will you explain each thing?

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:42.070
Let's start with the big 
hamburger. What's that?

00:09:42.070 --> 00:09:43.430
Aggressively greasy.

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:44.850
Tenaciously sweet.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:46.610
Harshly seasoned.

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:48.890
Tasting so bad for you, but so good!

00:09:50.470 --> 00:09:54.010
Um, well, what's it made of?

00:09:56.990 --> 00:09:58.600
These ingredients look very different

00:09:58.600 --> 00:10:00.120
from what we use in this world.

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:01.960
Cloned beef?

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:03.440
Genetically altered?

00:10:03.440 --> 00:10:05.090
Artificially flavored?

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:07.250
What's all that?

00:10:07.730 --> 00:10:10.310
I'm going to try to duplicate it.

00:10:10.870 --> 00:10:14.800
Princess, I'm afraid this will 
require various expenses.

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:17.480
He's useless in this state.

00:10:17.480 --> 00:10:18.910
Do whatever it takes.

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:21.740
Thank you so much.

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:38.290
That's a lot of food.

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:40.730
I'm going to try to make it from this.

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:43.370
Yeah!

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:45.070
First in Sapporo!

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:49.580
Kon, it looks like the big 
hamburger meal is done.

00:10:49.570 --> 00:10:50.750
Come eat it.

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:51.750
Come again?

00:10:58.340 --> 00:11:01.190
Could this possibly be...

00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:03.320
Don't rush it.

00:11:04.070 --> 00:11:05.760
Why don't you drink something first?

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:11.020
C-Cola?

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:33.900
Would you like another glass?

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:35.300
Yeah!

00:11:46.070 --> 00:11:48.150
Give me another one! Another one!

00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:49.840
What, you want seconds?

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:51.810
All right. Just a second.

00:11:53.680 --> 00:11:55.920
Oh, and some more fries, too.

00:11:56.970 --> 00:11:58.040
Sis?

00:11:58.040 --> 00:11:59.320
Hey, Marian.

00:12:04.130 --> 00:12:05.430
What is this?

00:12:28.570 --> 00:12:30.180
Stop right there, ingredients!

00:12:36.420 --> 00:12:38.320
Two hundred eleven.

00:12:38.870 --> 00:12:40.220
Two hundred twelve.

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:44.490
Hey, how was the big hamburger...

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:45.690
Kon?

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:49.120
Ba-ba-ba-ba!

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:50.810
Huh? Wrong spell?

00:12:50.810 --> 00:12:52.870
Reset!

00:12:57.660 --> 00:13:00.300
So where did you and 
Erec-sama go after that?

00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:00.930
To a hot spring.

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:02.260
What?! To a hot spring?

00:13:02.250 --> 00:13:03.490
That sounds good,

00:13:03.490 --> 00:13:05.560
getting into hot water and 
enduring it for a long time.

00:13:05.560 --> 00:13:07.360
You've got a one track mind.

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:11.880
So are you saying you got 
into a tub with Erec-sama?

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:15.940
No, he wanted to be alone.

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:17.290
I-I see.

00:13:17.290 --> 00:13:19.210
Sounds like, you know...

00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:20.260
I'll say it right now,

00:13:20.260 --> 00:13:22.200
Erec-sama would never go 
to a cheap hostess club.

00:13:22.200 --> 00:13:23.870
That's not all.

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:26.780
You know, there are plenty 
of gentlemen's places

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:28.940
around a hot spring resort 
that are ready to cater

00:13:28.940 --> 00:13:30.850
to the customer's every need, 
if you know what I mean.

00:13:30.850 --> 00:13:32.240
I told you it's not like that!

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:35.290
So where does he get 
his manly needs met?

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:38.400
You know, in fighting, that's where.

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:39.220
I see.

00:13:39.220 --> 00:13:40.650
That is so him.

00:13:40.650 --> 00:13:42.590
Putting his life on the line.

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:46.480
The splash of blood, 
the scream of the enemy.

00:13:46.480 --> 00:13:49.230
But he will not deliver 
the finishing blow yet.

00:13:49.230 --> 00:13:51.410
The fun is just beginning!

00:13:51.410 --> 00:13:53.190
The enemy is begging for his life,

00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:55.680
but he is killing him ever 
so slowly, bit by bit!

00:13:55.690 --> 00:13:57.400
That's you!

00:14:01.350 --> 00:14:03.900
I don't think the problem 
was with the taste.

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:07.360
But Kon's back in his la la land again.

00:14:10.050 --> 00:14:11.880
So we can't get any of those comics

00:14:11.880 --> 00:14:14.000
or whatever he wanted?

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:14.710
That's right.

00:14:14.710 --> 00:14:16.600
What is a comic, anyway?

00:14:16.600 --> 00:14:18.250
It seems to be like 
our illustrated sagas,

00:14:18.250 --> 00:14:20.380
but with many, many more pictures.

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:22.270
Is it different from a picture book?

00:14:22.270 --> 00:14:23.940
Apparently.

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:26.760
It is created for the young
 as well as older people.

00:14:26.780 --> 00:14:29.350
It makes you excited, anxious, nervous...

00:14:29.350 --> 00:14:32.060
Some of it is even erotic.

00:14:33.710 --> 00:14:36.000
Then it must be one of those...

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:39.400
You know, those picture books 
they make to excite adults.

00:14:40.420 --> 00:14:41.150
Here you go.

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:42.910
What's this?

00:14:42.910 --> 00:14:45.290
Our world's version of comics.

00:14:45.290 --> 00:14:48.700
Wow, you guys have comics, too?

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:50.620
Enjoy.

00:14:50.620 --> 00:14:51.700
What?

00:15:08.180 --> 00:15:10.640
Hadoken! Hadoken!

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:13.600
Rairaiken! Ownership rights! Franchise!

00:15:14.130 --> 00:15:16.030
I guess it wasn't the same thing.

00:15:16.030 --> 00:15:18.160
What on earth did you show him?

00:15:18.160 --> 00:15:18.950
I'm not telling.

00:15:18.950 --> 00:15:19.900
Oh jeez.

00:15:19.900 --> 00:15:21.260
What a bother.

00:15:21.260 --> 00:15:22.130
Senpukyaku!

00:15:22.430 --> 00:15:24.240
Drunk person! Sightseer!

00:15:24.240 --> 00:15:25.580
What are we going to do?

00:15:25.580 --> 00:15:27.990
It's like he's slipping 
further and further away.

00:15:27.990 --> 00:15:28.780
All right.

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:29.490
Sainglain?

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:31.910
Stop this make-believe gaming!

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:34.490
I'll take you to a real game.

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:36.490
A game?

00:15:39.270 --> 00:15:40.970
This is...

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:43.880
A place to unleash male spirit.

00:15:54.510 --> 00:15:57.450
Oh, so by gaming, you mean gambling.

00:15:57.450 --> 00:15:59.390
Let me warn you, 
the skills I gained from the

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:00.870
stripping games are nothing to sneeze at.

00:16:00.870 --> 00:16:02.070
Hey, Kon!

00:16:02.790 --> 00:16:04.210
I settled it.

00:16:04.210 --> 00:16:05.230
Over here.

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:10.740
<i>Why are we going downstairs?</i>

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:12.610
<i>Is this for the high stakes games?</i>

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:13.990
<i>Is this the VIP area?</i>

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:15.280
<i>Is this illegal?</i>

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:17.160
<i>Is that why we brought our weapons?</i>

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:23.410
Ladies and gentlemen, I thank 
you for your patience.

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:28.420
The first match of the MMA 
Championship will now begin!

00:16:29.210 --> 00:16:33.430
Champion Blood Heart!

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:39.930
Killer Boyanski!

00:16:40.210 --> 00:16:41.230
What is this place?

00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:42.260
An arena?

00:16:42.260 --> 00:16:44.900
That's right. You bet on the fight.

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:49.430
Next, we have Jack Hammer!

00:16:50.290 --> 00:16:52.090
Who's the headliner?

00:16:52.090 --> 00:16:54.010
I'm guessing it would be Blood Heart.

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:56.580
He's going to fight with a chainsaw?

00:16:56.580 --> 00:16:58.250
That's just for publicity.

00:16:58.250 --> 00:16:59.890
He won't have one in the match.

00:16:59.890 --> 00:17:01.500
That makes sense.

00:17:01.880 --> 00:17:06.300
And Bear Light!

00:17:07.110 --> 00:17:10.130
Our referee tonight 
is Kottessa Yamamoto.

00:17:14.610 --> 00:17:15.820
Who'd you put your money on?

00:17:15.820 --> 00:17:17.070
I'm not telling.

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:19.760
But if he wins, I'll buy you dinner.

00:17:19.780 --> 00:17:21.110
What about me?

00:17:21.110 --> 00:17:23.140
You can't bet.

00:17:34.790 --> 00:17:39.660
And the winner is Blood Heart!

00:17:39.960 --> 00:17:43.170
Hey, how come I can't buy a ticket?

00:17:43.170 --> 00:17:44.590
That's because...

00:17:45.360 --> 00:17:47.170
The second match is about to begin.

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:48.910
If you're participating,

00:17:48.910 --> 00:17:51.180
please enter the ring 
when I call your name.

00:17:51.810 --> 00:17:53.360
Jack Rantan.

00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:57.160
Skull Murder.

00:17:57.160 --> 00:17:58.640
I'm counting on you.

00:17:58.640 --> 00:18:00.430
Yeah. I got this.

00:18:00.840 --> 00:18:02.040
Gallbone.

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:04.310
We'll split the winnings fifty-fifty.

00:18:04.310 --> 00:18:04.930
Sure.

00:18:06.370 --> 00:18:09.940
And then I have a foreigner, 
Kon Battler Five.

00:18:13.620 --> 00:18:16.200
Huh? What? What's going on?

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:20.200
See, participants aren't 
allowed to place bets.

00:18:20.800 --> 00:18:22.700
Is this a joke?

00:18:27.210 --> 00:18:28.210
Stay back!

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:29.920
Just one more match.

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:32.360
There's no one here who 
can stand up against me.

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:34.860
We have your opponent 
for the deciding match.

00:18:35.610 --> 00:18:36.660
Who is it?

00:18:36.660 --> 00:18:38.220
Kon Battler Five.

00:18:38.470 --> 00:18:41.020
What? How was the match?

00:18:41.860 --> 00:18:45.790
He kept running away, 
then climbed up on the net

00:18:45.790 --> 00:18:47.940
and let the remaining 
three players duke it out.

00:18:47.940 --> 00:18:50.100
When there was just one 
exhausted man standing...

00:18:50.100 --> 00:18:53.110
<i>Nut Kick!</i>

00:18:59.070 --> 00:19:00.240
Hey, hey!

00:19:01.810 --> 00:19:03.620
We can't underestimate him.

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:08.840
The handlers have come to an agreement.

00:19:08.840 --> 00:19:11.010
The final match will now begin!

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:14.390
But what's this?

00:19:14.390 --> 00:19:17.010
It looks like Blood Heart has 
brought out his chainsaw!

00:19:17.710 --> 00:19:20.620
And it looks like Kon Battler Five

00:19:20.620 --> 00:19:22.960
has conferred with the referee.

00:19:25.780 --> 00:19:28.920
Just now, I have gotten an 
objection from Kon Battler Five,

00:19:28.920 --> 00:19:30.590
who claims the use of a chainsaw

00:19:30.590 --> 00:19:32.610
is too dangerous in this match.

00:19:33.040 --> 00:19:36.740
Blood Heart rebuts that Kon 
Battler Five has brought

00:19:36.740 --> 00:19:38.880
a sword to this match.

00:19:38.880 --> 00:19:41.630
As the referee, I have deemed 
Blood Heart's opinion

00:19:41.630 --> 00:19:43.230
to be fair.

00:19:43.230 --> 00:19:45.780
The chainsaw will be allowed.

00:19:48.690 --> 00:19:49.790
Really?!

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:54.630
What are you doing?!

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:57.050
You won against Erec!

00:19:57.050 --> 00:19:58.500
I can't, I can't!

00:19:58.510 --> 00:20:00.550
This guy and Erec are 
two different breeds!

00:20:04.060 --> 00:20:05.360
Fight! Win!

00:20:05.360 --> 00:20:06.180
Victory is yours!

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:08.180
Second place isn't good enough?

00:20:08.180 --> 00:20:08.900
No!

00:20:08.900 --> 00:20:09.590
No!

00:20:09.590 --> 00:20:11.690
Are you trying to make me lose money?!

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:13.650
Well, why'd you bet on me?!

00:20:40.570 --> 00:20:41.970
You got this!

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:42.890
It's in the bag!

00:20:42.890 --> 00:20:44.130
Finish him!

00:20:48.900 --> 00:20:50.930
All right, I give up!

00:20:52.500 --> 00:20:53.890
What?!

00:21:02.410 --> 00:21:04.260
I get it!

00:21:04.260 --> 00:21:06.610
If I show any weakness 
around you guys, I'll die!

00:21:06.610 --> 00:21:07.760
You'll kill me!

00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:09.710
So I got a little homesick!

00:21:09.710 --> 00:21:11.210
So you guys feed me weird stuff,

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:13.210
make me lose face in 
front of the crowd,

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:13.210
His chances were good, too.

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:15.170
and even put my life on the line!

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:15.960
And I lost big.

00:21:15.980 --> 00:21:18.520
Let's go back to our rooms and rest.

00:21:16.630 --> 00:21:18.640
I can't even peacefully escape reality for a bit!

00:21:18.500 --> 00:21:19.340
Sounds good.

00:21:19.340 --> 00:21:22.010
Hey, wait! What the hell 
is wrong with you guys?

00:21:22.010 --> 00:21:24.530
You gonna just pretend none 
of this even happened?

00:21:24.530 --> 00:21:27.160
A little consideration, 
okay? That's all I ask!

00:23:08.370 --> 00:23:10.670
So I guess we'll finally be fighting

00:23:10.670 --> 00:23:12.170
our arch-nemesis DT next week.

00:23:12.170 --> 00:23:16.250
Erec-sama brought the DDOS 
weapons home, as well.

00:23:16.250 --> 00:23:20.200
With those we can be on par with 
the battle power of Hyperions.

00:23:20.200 --> 00:23:23.110
Yes, we'll get one step 
closer to Erec-sama.

00:23:23.110 --> 00:23:24.370
That reminds me.

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:26.880
Does anyone know what 
exactly a Hyperion is?

00:23:26.880 --> 00:23:27.740
Huh?

00:23:27.740 --> 00:23:32.470
Well, it's... It's a 
chosen warrior, like Erec-sama.

00:23:32.470 --> 00:23:34.820
But DT is also a Hyperion.

00:23:34.820 --> 00:23:36.820
W-Well...

00:23:36.820 --> 00:23:38.510
Are you saying he's also a New Type?

00:23:38.510 --> 00:23:39.380
No!

00:23:39.390 --> 00:23:41.440
Anyway, it's something quite amazing...

00:23:41.440 --> 00:23:42.400
What?

00:23:42.400 --> 00:23:44.400
Anyway, it's something quite amazing!

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:45.520
You just said what he said.

00:23:45.520 --> 00:23:48.110
Anyway, it's something <i>quite</i> amazing!

00:23:48.120 --> 00:23:49.550
You said the same thing, 
just in a different tone.

00:23:49.550 --> 00:23:52.700
Then what, Gustave? 
You know something we don't?

00:23:52.700 --> 00:23:53.950
You bet I do.

00:23:54.450 --> 00:23:58.950
Any<i>way</i>, it is <i>something</i> quite ama<i>zing</i>!

00:23:58.950 --> 00:24:00.560
We just said that!

00:24:04.480 --> 00:24:08.160
By the way, why are 
we playing volleyball?

00:24:08.630 --> 00:24:09.880
Uh....

00:24:09.880 --> 00:24:13.010
After spending the night 
in a dilapidated castle,

00:24:09.880 --> 00:24:24.810
<b>Next Time</b>

00:24:13.010 --> 00:24:15.750
we are ambushed by Incognito.

00:24:15.750 --> 00:24:17.270
What are those weapons?

00:24:17.270 --> 00:24:18.890
Are those new?!

00:24:18.890 --> 00:24:20.270
Stop!

00:24:20.270 --> 00:24:23.560
I don't want to die a virgin!

00:24:24.810 --> 00:24:30.320
Erec had not only received the Alma Gear

00:24:24.810 --> 00:24:30.320
"Calibre" from the mysterious woman,

00:24:30.320 --> 00:24:34.650
but also "DDOS", a new type of weapon

00:24:30.320 --> 00:24:34.650
that even normal people can use.
